egressed. Gates: red int363_ splitter tests, the splitter rule, the handoff in try_shell_construct, the notice, a box nsh -c versus bash -c proof, four nsh-test conformance cases, then the laptop. Limits stated: on dash, time ( ) is a syntax error where it was an untimed run; a ( ) & started by sh is not an nsh job; the destructive-command guard does not look inside ( ) groups or for loops, before and after, and that is a separate intent. Out of scope: brace groups (next intent), process substitution, time without a group, wait, function definitions, if ...; fi | cmd, the bare (case ...) group, $(a; b), ${VAR:-x}, the guard gap, try_grouping, the spine, exec.rs and expand.rs. Bumps are novashell patch (6.1.4 to 6.1.5) and nsh-test patch (2.2.4 to 2.2.5). Agents push branch int-363 only; Eric reviews; Christian merges, seals, ships and runs doors and d on the laptop.
